Ported from IDOL's vendored copy (IDOL 1364), where it was found and fixed.

The generated docs (AGENTS.md block, .pidly/README.md "## Claiming")
told agents to claim with `PIDLY_PID=$$ pidly claim 7`. $$ is the shell
running the command. A harness that runs each command in a fresh shell
(Claude Code does) ends that shell when the call returns, so the claim
reads dead at once: the agent's own release fails and anyone may reap it.

Fix: recommend plain `pidly claim 7`, which names $CLAUDE_PID or the
process that ran pidly, and say not to prefix PIDLY_PID=$$; PIDLY_PID is
for a wrapper that knows a longer-lived process to name. Same in README.md.

Done when agents.sh fails on a generated document that recommends
PIDLY_PID=$$.
